Let $F$ be either $\mathbb R$ or $\mathbb C$, with conjugation equal to the identity on $\mathbb R$ and with complex conjugation as in [[def-complex-conjugate-real-imaginary-part-and-modulus]]. An **inner product** on an $F$-vector space $V$ is a function $\langle\,\cdot\,,\,\cdot\,\rangle:V\times V\to F$ such that for all $u,v,w\in V$ and $a,b\in F$:

1. $\langle au+bv,w\rangle=a\langle u,w\rangle+b\langle v,w\rangle$;
2. $\langle u,v\rangle=\overline{\langle v,u\rangle}$;
3. $\langle v,v\rangle$ is real and nonnegative, and $\langle v,v\rangle=0$ if and only if $v=0$.

The first two clauses imply conjugate-linearity in the second argument: $\langle u,av+bw\rangle=\overline a\langle u,v\rangle+\overline b\langle u,w\rangle$. This is the linear-first convention of [[def-sesquilinear-and-hermitian-forms-over-a-field-with-involution]]. A vector space equipped with an inner product is an **inner product space**.

Let $R$ be a commutative ring with unit and let $\delta\in R$. Use the quantum integers $[0]=0$, $[1]=1$, $[r+1]=\delta[r]-[r-1]$ of [[def-temperley-lieb-quantum-integers-and-quantum-characteristic]]. Put $p_0=1_0$ and $p_1=1_1$. For $r\ge1$, if $p_r$ is defined and $[r+1]$ is a unit, put

$$P_r=p_r\otimes1_1\in\mathrm{TL}_{r+1}(R,\delta),\qquad p_{r+1}=P_r-\frac{[r]}{[r+1]}P_rU_rP_r,$$

where $U_r$ is the cap-cup generator on the final two of the $r+1$ strands in [[def-temperley-lieb-diagram-category]]. Thus $p_n$ is defined by this recursion only when every $[2],\ldots,[n]$ is a unit. The definition makes no assertion that failure of a denominator condition prevents every other normalized projector from existing.

```tikz
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.9cm,y=0.9cm]
  \draw (0,0) -- (0,1.8);
  \draw (1,0) -- (1,1.8);
  \node[draw,minimum width=0.55cm,minimum height=0.45cm] at (0.5,1.25) {$p_r$};
  \node[draw,minimum width=0.55cm,minimum height=0.45cm] at (0.5,0.45) {$p_r$};
  \draw (2,0) .. controls (2,0.55) and (3,0.55) .. (3,0);
  \draw (2,1.8) .. controls (2,1.25) and (3,1.25) .. (3,1.8);
\end{tikzpicture}
```

The box labels stand for the corresponding idempotents and the right-hand cup-cap is $U_r$; the picture is only a convention aid. All algebraic identities are proved from the labeled matching composition and the relations of [[lem-temperley-lieb-generators-satisfy-local-relations]].

